def rep(p,a,b):
    s=open(p).read(); assert s.count(a)==1,(p,a[:70]); open(p,'w').write(s.replace(a,b))
rep('CHANGELOG.md',"kern reads the snapshot as text and never runs it; a missing, unreadable or unparseable snapshot changes nothing.",
"kern reads the snapshot as text and never runs it; a missing, unreadable or unparseable snapshot changes nothing. It caches the parsed table in its state dir, keyed by the snapshot's path, size and modification time, and reads the cache as data the same way; a forged cache, like a forged snapshot, can only add votes.")
rep('docs/plans/contract.md',"Nothing from the snapshot is evaluated: awk reads at most its first 4 MB as text. A missing, unreadable or unparseable snapshot sets nothing, and no failure stops the hook.",
"Nothing from the snapshot is evaluated: awk reads at most its first 4 MB as text. A missing, unreadable or unparseable snapshot sets nothing, and no failure stops the hook. The parsed table is cached in `$(state_dir)/aliases.cache` (mode 0600, written to a `mktemp` file in that dir and renamed over the cache): a first line `kern aliases <_ALIASES_CACHE_V> <length of _ALIASES_AWK><TAB><snapshot path><TAB><size> <mtime>`, then the `<hex><TAB>expansion` lines. A cache whose first line differs is rebuilt; a symlinked cache file or state dir is never read or written through; a cache that cannot be written is skipped silently.\n- `_alias_key FILE`: prints FILE's size and modification time in seconds (BSD or GNU `stat`); exit 1 when neither reads it.\n- `_alias_table`: reads `<hex><TAB>expansion` lines on stdin into `_KA_<hex>` as data, the way `aliases_load` reads the parse and the cache: a line whose name is not hex digits is skipped, and reading stops after 4 MB.")
